dir<0 (up): I'm inserting "target" before "item" — if target is already the previous sibling, this becomes a no-op! Correct is: `ul.insertBefore(item, target)` (item before previous).

dir>0 (down): `ul.insertBefore(item, target.nextElementSibling)` = item after target ✓ correct.

Fix: `if (dir < 0) ul.insertBefore(item, target);` — symmetric! Why did ArrowDown work, and did ArrowUp "work" in earlier runs?? In previous successful keyboard runs (according to the summary "keyboard reordering works correctly")... well, the ArrowDown direction was working. The up direction was silently a no-op.

Fix moveByKey:
```js
function moveByKey(item, dir) {
  const ul = item.parentElement;
  const target = dir < 0 ? item.previousElementSibling : item.nextElementSibling;
  if (!target) return;
  flipChildren(ul, function () {
    if (dir < 0) ul.insertBefore(item, target);
    else ul.insertBefore(target, item);
  });
  item.focus();
}
```
(insertBefore(target, item) = target after item = item before target... wait, for dir>0: item after target: insertBefore(target, item)?? That inserts target before item → item after target ✓. And dir<0: item before target: insertBefore(item, target) ✓. Both symmetric and readable!)

